    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **17 run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp09Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment feature, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, across the standard Spring layers:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field mapped to a new `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four schema variants (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`). The tests run against `hsqldb`.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it into the GET response (no mapper change needed since it maps by name).\n\n4. **Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 assign the code on create, before `saveOwner`, via a `nextCustomerCode` helper:\n   - **LAST3** = first three letters of `lastName`, upper-cased (`Locale.ROOT`).\n   - **NNNN** = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits (`%04d`).\n\nSince assignment happens per create and the count reflects previously-persisted owners (JPA auto-flushes before the query), each new owner's sequence is exactly one greater than the previous \u2014 satisfying the test's global-sequence assertion (e.g. `SMI-0011` then `JON-0012`).",
